{"success":true,"rounds":[{"id":"round-1","number":1,"title":"The Garage Days","level":"Beginner","tagline":"Home-Cooked Delivery in Karachi · Genesis of the Startup","story":"Two friends start a small home-cooked food delivery service in Karachi. They have 10 customers and 5 partnered home-kitchen restaurants initially, operating out of a garage with manual spreadsheets.","task":"Design a clean, normalized relational database covering customers, orders, menu items, and order deliveries. Implement baseline entity integrity and relational constraints.","skills":["Entity-Relationship Diagrams (ERDs)","1NF, 2NF, 3NF Normalization","Core SQL CREATE TABLE Statements","Primary Keys & Foreign Keys","1:1 and 1:M Relationships"],"requiresCodeStorage":true,"venueType":"Online","date":"22 October 2026","scaleStats":{"customers":"10 active eaters","restaurants":"5 home chefs"},"judgePdf":{"filename":"CodeConnect26_Round1_TheGarageDays_Brief.pdf","uploadedAt":"08 Oct 2026, 14:30 PKT","uploadedBy":"Lead Judge (UBIT DB Panel)","url":"/docs/round1_brief.pdf","size":"1.4 MB"}},{"id":"round-2","number":2,"title":"The Expansion","level":"Intermediate","tagline":"Cross-City Scale · Riders, Ratings & Multi-Channel Payments","story":"The startup explodes in popularity, scaling to 5,000 customers across 3 major cities. Operations now involve hundreds of independent restaurants, real-time dispatch riders, customer rating reviews, and multiple payment gateways (Cash, JazzCash, EasyPaisa, Cards).","task":"Upgrade the database architecture to support many-to-many relationships, dynamic rider assignments, complex billing transactions, and query speedups through composite indexing.","skills":["Complex M:M & Self-referencing Relationships","Normalization to BCNF / 4NF","Targeted Indexing & Execution Plans","Complex Query Writing (Joins, Aggregations, Subqueries)","ACID Transactions & Stored Procedures / Views"],"requiresCodeStorage":true,"venueType":"Online","date":"23 October 2026","scaleStats":{"customers":"5,000 customers","restaurants":"3 cities / 120 hubs","riders":"350 active riders"},"judgePdf":{"filename":"CodeConnect26_Round2_TheExpansion_Rubric.pdf","uploadedAt":"08 Oct 2026, 19:15 PKT","uploadedBy":"Lead Judge (UBIT DB Panel)","url":"/docs/round2_rubric.pdf","size":"2.1 MB"}},{"id":"round-3","number":3,"title":"The Platform","level":"Advanced","tagline":"Peak Ramadan / Eid Rush · 1M Users & Hyper-Scale Architecture","story":"The startup is now Karachi’s premier food delivery platform, serving 1,000,000 users with 500 top-tier restaurants and 2,000 delivery riders. The database must survive extreme concurrent spike loads during Ramadan Sehri/Iftar and Eid night rushes without downtime.","task":"Architect a resilient high-throughput infrastructure. Plan partitioning, read/write sharding, caching tiers (Redis/Memcached), evaluate SQL vs NoSQL trade-offs, and defend concurrency and disaster-recovery trade-offs live on campus.","skills":["Horizontal Sharding & Read-Replicas","Table Partitioning & Cold/Warm Tiering","NoSQL vs SQL Hybrid Architecture Decisions","Caching & Invalidation Strategies","Concurrency Control, Pessimistic/Optimistic Locking","CAP Theorem Trade-Offs & Live Defense Pitch"],"requiresCodeStorage":false,"venueType":"On-Campus","date":"24 October 2026","scaleStats":{"customers":"1,000,000+ users","restaurants":"500+ commercial partners","riders":"2,000 full-fleet riders"},"judgePdf":{"filename":"CodeConnect26_Round3_ThePlatform_Defense_Rubric.pdf","uploadedAt":"09 Oct 2026, 06:00 PKT","uploadedBy":"Head of Jury (UBIT UoK)","url":"/docs/round3_defense.pdf","size":"2.8 MB"}}]}